\boxed{\textbf{Preemption Residue}}

When a system predicts a continuation before receiving confirming information, save the prediction. Then when the actual continuation arrives:

\Delta =
\text{actual continuation}
-
\text{predicted continuation}.

That delta tells us how much was already encoded in the preceding pattern versus how much genuinely new information arrived.

Guess first. Seal the guess. Then reveal.

